1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,706
Sweetheart, in nineteen sixty-seven,

2
00:00:02,706 --> 00:00:05,337
every party in America had a little

3
00:00:05,337 --> 00:00:08,343
pot of Swedish meatballs keeping warm on

4
00:00:08,343 --> 00:00:11,050
a table, with a basket of toothpicks

5
00:00:11,050 --> 00:00:11,877
next to it.

6
00:00:12,057 --> 00:00:15,269
Little round meatballs in a creamy brown

7
00:00:15,269 --> 00:00:17,838
gravy, with a whisper of nutmeg.

8
00:00:18,018 --> 00:00:20,915
People stood around that pot all night,

9
00:00:20,915 --> 00:00:23,218
spearing them one at a time and

10
00:00:23,218 --> 00:00:25,669
telling themselves just one more.

11
00:00:25,849 --> 00:00:27,955
I never saw that pot go home

12
00:00:27,955 --> 00:00:29,460
with anything in it.

13
00:00:29,810 --> 00:00:32,782
But people tell me their meatballs come

14
00:00:32,782 --> 00:00:34,535
out hard as golf balls,

15
00:00:34,535 --> 00:00:35,602
or dry inside,

16
00:00:35,602 --> 00:00:37,813
or the gravy is thin and gray

17
00:00:37,813 --> 00:00:38,575
and lumpy.

18
00:00:38,755 --> 00:00:41,147
So tonight I'm giving you Mrs.

19
00:00:41,327 --> 00:00:43,768
Lindqvist's Swedish meatballs,

20
00:00:43,768 --> 00:00:45,477
a real family supper,

21
00:00:45,477 --> 00:00:48,570
every step, and the five mistakes that

22
00:00:48,570 --> 00:00:49,790
make them hard.

23
00:00:49,970 --> 00:00:51,261
And stay with me,

24
00:00:51,261 --> 00:00:53,766
because the last secret is in the

25
00:00:53,766 --> 00:00:55,967
gravy, and it's a jar most of

26
00:00:55,967 --> 00:00:58,016
us have in the icebox door.

27
00:00:58,366 --> 00:00:59,457
Mrs.

28
00:00:59,637 --> 00:01:03,055
Lindqvist, the Swedish widow from our church

29
00:01:03,055 --> 00:01:05,929
in Mansfield, made them every Sunday.

30
00:01:06,109 --> 00:01:08,860
In Swedish they're called kottbullar,

31
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:11,759
and every grandmother in Sweden has her

32
00:01:11,759 --> 00:01:12,576
own recipe.

33
00:01:12,756 --> 00:01:14,010
Hers were small,

34
00:01:14,010 --> 00:01:16,126
about the size of a walnut,

35
00:01:16,126 --> 00:01:17,458
soft as a pillow,

36
00:01:17,458 --> 00:01:19,966
and served with mashed potatoes,

37
00:01:19,966 --> 00:01:21,690
the brown cream gravy,

38
00:01:21,690 --> 00:01:24,276
and a spoon of lingonberry jam on

39
00:01:24,276 --> 00:01:24,982
the side.

40
00:01:25,162 --> 00:01:27,681
I'd never seen jam with meat.

41
00:01:27,861 --> 00:01:30,020
I thought she'd lost her mind.

42
00:01:30,371 --> 00:01:31,975
Then I tasted it,

43
00:01:31,975 --> 00:01:32,542
honey.

44
00:01:32,722 --> 00:01:35,749
The sweet, tart berries with the rich,

45
00:01:35,749 --> 00:01:38,457
salty gravy and the soft meatball.

46
00:01:38,637 --> 00:01:40,801
It was the best bite I'd had

47
00:01:40,801 --> 00:01:42,115
in my whole life,

48
00:01:42,115 --> 00:01:43,815
at fourteen years old.

49
00:01:43,995 --> 00:01:46,476
I went home and asked my mother

50
00:01:46,476 --> 00:01:48,797
to put grape jelly on our pot

51
00:01:48,797 --> 00:01:49,278
roast.

52
00:01:49,458 --> 00:01:50,793
She said no,

53
00:01:50,793 --> 00:01:52,128
very firmly.

54
00:01:52,308 --> 00:01:55,012
In a minute I'll tell you why

55
00:01:55,012 --> 00:01:55,384
Mrs.

56
00:01:55,564 --> 00:01:58,222
Lindqvist's meatballs were so soft,

57
00:01:58,222 --> 00:02:01,184
and it's something from your bread box.

58
00:02:01,534 --> 00:02:02,823
And they're cheap,

59
00:02:02,823 --> 00:02:03,612
sweetheart.

60
00:02:03,792 --> 00:02:05,618
A pound and a half of meat

61
00:02:05,618 --> 00:02:08,077
makes about forty little meatballs,

62
00:02:08,077 --> 00:02:10,607
enough for six people with potatoes.

63
00:02:10,787 --> 00:02:14,165
The whole supper costs about fourteen dollars.

64
00:02:14,345 --> 00:02:16,266
And they freeze beautifully,

65
00:02:16,266 --> 00:02:18,324
so you can make a double batch

66
00:02:18,324 --> 00:02:20,862
on a Sunday afternoon and have supper

67
00:02:20,862 --> 00:02:23,331
ready for two busy weeknights later.

68
00:02:23,681 --> 00:02:25,307
Here's what you need,

69
00:02:25,307 --> 00:02:25,771
honey.

70
00:02:25,951 --> 00:02:28,332
One pound of ground beef and half

71
00:02:28,332 --> 00:02:29,992
a pound of ground pork.

72
00:02:30,172 --> 00:02:32,004
Half a small onion,

73
00:02:32,004 --> 00:02:32,679
grated.

74
00:02:32,859 --> 00:02:35,209
Two slices of white bread,

75
00:02:35,209 --> 00:02:37,016
crusts off, torn up.

76
00:02:37,196 --> 00:02:39,146
A third of a cup of milk.

77
00:02:39,326 --> 00:02:40,522
One egg.

78
00:02:40,702 --> 00:02:42,336
One teaspoon of salt,

79
00:02:42,336 --> 00:02:44,359
half a teaspoon of pepper,

80
00:02:44,359 --> 00:02:47,237
and a quarter teaspoon each of nutmeg

81
00:02:47,237 --> 00:02:48,248
and allspice.

82
00:02:48,428 --> 00:02:51,306
Those two spices are what make them

83
00:02:51,306 --> 00:02:52,457
taste Swedish.

84
00:02:52,807 --> 00:02:54,270
For the gravy.

85
00:02:54,450 --> 00:02:56,796
Three tablespoons of butter.

86
00:02:56,976 --> 00:02:59,344
Three tablespoons of flour.

87
00:02:59,524 --> 00:03:01,474
Two cups of beef broth.

88
00:03:01,654 --> 00:03:03,841
Three quarters of a cup of heavy

89
00:03:03,841 --> 00:03:05,207
cream or sour cream.

90
00:03:05,387 --> 00:03:08,429
A tablespoon of soy sauce or Worcestershire.

91
00:03:08,609 --> 00:03:10,620
And the secret ingredient,

92
00:03:10,620 --> 00:03:12,245
from the icebox door,

93
00:03:12,245 --> 00:03:14,720
which I'll tell you about at the

94
00:03:14,720 --> 00:03:15,029
end.

95
00:03:15,209 --> 00:03:19,050
For serving, mashed potatoes or egg noodles,

96
00:03:19,050 --> 00:03:22,106
and lingonberry or cranberry sauce.

97
00:03:22,455 --> 00:03:25,339
Step one, and here's the secret from

98
00:03:25,339 --> 00:03:26,461
the bread box.

99
00:03:26,641 --> 00:03:28,813
Put the torn bread in a big

100
00:03:28,813 --> 00:03:31,066
bowl, pour the milk over it,

101
00:03:31,066 --> 00:03:33,640
and let it sit for five minutes,

102
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:35,732
until it's soft and mushy.

103
00:03:35,912 --> 00:03:37,653
Then mash it with a fork.

104
00:03:37,833 --> 00:03:39,886
That's called a panade,

105
00:03:39,886 --> 00:03:40,422
honey.

106
00:03:40,602 --> 00:03:43,656
Mistake number one is using dry bread

107
00:03:43,656 --> 00:03:45,885
crumbs, or no bread at all.

108
00:03:46,065 --> 00:03:48,847
The milky bread is what keeps the

109
00:03:48,847 --> 00:03:51,544
meatballs soft and juicy inside.

110
00:03:51,894 --> 00:03:53,718
And grate the onion,

111
00:03:53,718 --> 00:03:54,994
don't chop it.

112
00:03:55,174 --> 00:03:57,626
Use the big holes of a box

113
00:03:57,626 --> 00:03:58,286
grater.

114
00:03:58,466 --> 00:04:01,455
Mistake number two is big chunks of

115
00:04:01,455 --> 00:04:02,309
raw onion.

116
00:04:02,489 --> 00:04:04,766
They don't cook through in a small

117
00:04:04,766 --> 00:04:07,578
meatball, and they make the meatballs fall

118
00:04:07,578 --> 00:04:07,980
apart.

119
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:11,063
Grated onion melts right into the meat

120
00:04:11,063 --> 00:04:12,514
and keeps it moist.

121
00:04:12,694 --> 00:04:13,658
Mrs.

122
00:04:13,838 --> 00:04:16,604
Lindqvist cooked her grated onion in a

123
00:04:16,604 --> 00:04:18,060
little butter first,

124
00:04:18,060 --> 00:04:19,225
so it was sweet.

125
00:04:19,405 --> 00:04:20,531
I do too.

126
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:21,856
Step two.

127
00:04:22,036 --> 00:04:23,226
Add the meat,

128
00:04:23,226 --> 00:04:24,966
the onion, the egg,

129
00:04:24,966 --> 00:04:26,523
the salt, pepper,

130
00:04:26,523 --> 00:04:30,186
nutmeg and allspice to the soaked bread.

131
00:04:30,366 --> 00:04:33,164
And now mistake number three.

132
00:04:33,344 --> 00:04:34,981
Mixing it too hard.

133
00:04:35,161 --> 00:04:37,478
If you squeeze and knead the meat

134
00:04:37,478 --> 00:04:38,671
like bread dough,

135
00:04:38,671 --> 00:04:41,128
the meatballs turn dense and tough.

136
00:04:41,308 --> 00:04:43,952
Mix it gently with your fingertips,

137
00:04:43,952 --> 00:04:44,708
or a fork,

138
00:04:44,708 --> 00:04:47,276
just until everything is together.

139
00:04:47,456 --> 00:04:49,557
Stop the minute it looks even.

140
00:04:49,907 --> 00:04:51,613
If this is helping you,

141
00:04:51,613 --> 00:04:54,133
honey, tap the like button for me.

142
00:04:54,313 --> 00:04:57,100
It helps Grandma more than you know.

143
00:04:57,280 --> 00:04:59,815
Now wet your hands with cold water,

144
00:04:59,815 --> 00:05:01,698
so the meat doesn't stick,

145
00:05:01,698 --> 00:05:04,305
and roll the meatballs about an inch

146
00:05:04,305 --> 00:05:06,405
across, the size of a walnut.

147
00:05:06,585 --> 00:05:08,637
Keep them all the same size,

148
00:05:08,637 --> 00:05:10,103
so they cook evenly.

149
00:05:10,283 --> 00:05:11,978
Set them on a tray.

150
00:05:12,158 --> 00:05:13,398
If you have time,

151
00:05:13,398 --> 00:05:15,585
chill them for thirty minutes,

152
00:05:15,585 --> 00:05:17,846
so they hold their shape in the

153
00:05:17,846 --> 00:05:18,137
pan.

154
00:05:18,487 --> 00:05:19,544
Mrs.

155
00:05:19,724 --> 00:05:23,136
Lindqvist could roll forty meatballs in about

156
00:05:23,136 --> 00:05:25,335
six minutes, perfectly round,

157
00:05:25,335 --> 00:05:28,217
while talking the whole time about the

158
00:05:28,217 --> 00:05:29,430
pastor's sermon.

159
00:05:29,610 --> 00:05:31,409
I timed her once.

160
00:05:31,589 --> 00:05:33,194
It takes me fifteen,

161
00:05:33,194 --> 00:05:35,200
and mine aren't as round.

162
00:05:35,380 --> 00:05:36,444
She said, Ruth,

163
00:05:36,444 --> 00:05:37,720
roll them lightly,

164
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:39,989
like you're holding a baby bird.

165
00:05:40,169 --> 00:05:42,816
Squeeze them, and they'll be tough.

166
00:05:42,996 --> 00:05:45,517
I still hear her voice every time

167
00:05:45,517 --> 00:05:46,433
I make them.

168
00:05:46,782 --> 00:05:47,990
Step three.

169
00:05:48,170 --> 00:05:50,543
Melt a tablespoon of butter with a

170
00:05:50,543 --> 00:05:52,916
tablespoon of oil in a big skillet

171
00:05:52,916 --> 00:05:54,103
over medium heat.

172
00:05:54,283 --> 00:05:56,522
Add the meatballs in one layer,

173
00:05:56,522 --> 00:05:58,184
with room between them.

174
00:05:58,364 --> 00:06:01,382
Mistake number four is crowding the pan.

175
00:06:01,562 --> 00:06:02,844
Too many at once,

176
00:06:02,844 --> 00:06:05,482
and they steam instead of browning,

177
00:06:05,482 --> 00:06:06,914
and they turn gray.

178
00:06:07,094 --> 00:06:08,650
Cook them in batches,

179
00:06:08,650 --> 00:06:10,132
turning them gently,

180
00:06:10,132 --> 00:06:12,281
until they're brown all over,

181
00:06:12,281 --> 00:06:14,281
about eight to ten minutes.

182
00:06:14,630 --> 00:06:17,230
Shake the pan instead of turning each

183
00:06:17,230 --> 00:06:18,354
one with a fork,

184
00:06:18,354 --> 00:06:18,775
honey.

185
00:06:18,955 --> 00:06:21,433
They roll around and brown on all

186
00:06:21,433 --> 00:06:23,460
sides, and they stay round.

187
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:25,815
Take them out onto a plate when

188
00:06:25,815 --> 00:06:26,798
they're brown.

189
00:06:26,978 --> 00:06:29,038
They don't have to be cooked all

190
00:06:29,038 --> 00:06:30,326
the way through yet,

191
00:06:30,326 --> 00:06:32,643
because they'll finish in the gravy.

192
00:06:32,823 --> 00:06:34,727
And don't wash that pan.

193
00:06:34,907 --> 00:06:37,226
All those brown bits are the start

194
00:06:37,226 --> 00:06:38,112
of the gravy.

195
00:06:38,461 --> 00:06:40,447
Step four, the gravy.

196
00:06:40,627 --> 00:06:41,957
In the same pan,

197
00:06:41,957 --> 00:06:44,702
melt three tablespoons of butter.

198
00:06:44,882 --> 00:06:47,256
Whisk in the flour and cook it,

199
00:06:47,256 --> 00:06:49,936
stirring, for two or three minutes,

200
00:06:49,936 --> 00:06:52,157
until it turns a light brown,

201
00:06:52,157 --> 00:06:53,613
like peanut butter.

202
00:06:53,793 --> 00:06:56,540
Then slowly whisk in the beef broth,

203
00:06:56,540 --> 00:06:59,211
scraping up all the brown bits from

204
00:06:59,211 --> 00:07:00,050
the bottom.

205
00:07:00,230 --> 00:07:02,774
Let it bubble until it thickens,

206
00:07:02,774 --> 00:07:04,363
about three minutes.

207
00:07:04,543 --> 00:07:06,877
Then stir in the cream and the

208
00:07:06,877 --> 00:07:07,655
soy sauce.

209
00:07:08,004 --> 00:07:09,943
And mistake number five,

210
00:07:09,943 --> 00:07:11,638
the lumpy gray gravy.

211
00:07:11,818 --> 00:07:14,430
It comes from pouring all the broth

212
00:07:14,430 --> 00:07:16,369
in at once into raw flour.

213
00:07:16,549 --> 00:07:18,578
Cook the flour first,

214
00:07:18,578 --> 00:07:20,316
until it's golden,

215
00:07:20,316 --> 00:07:22,248
so it tastes toasty,

216
00:07:22,248 --> 00:07:23,214
not pasty.

217
00:07:23,394 --> 00:07:25,837
And pour the broth in slowly,

218
00:07:25,837 --> 00:07:27,438
a little at a time,

219
00:07:27,438 --> 00:07:28,618
whisking hard.

220
00:07:28,798 --> 00:07:30,432
If you get lumps anyway,

221
00:07:30,432 --> 00:07:32,270
pour it through a strainer,

222
00:07:32,270 --> 00:07:34,585
or whisk like your life depends on

223
00:07:34,585 --> 00:07:34,789
it.

224
00:07:34,969 --> 00:07:36,049
Mrs.

225
00:07:36,229 --> 00:07:38,850
Lindqvist never had a lump in her

226
00:07:38,850 --> 00:07:39,247
life.

227
00:07:39,597 --> 00:07:41,856
Now put the meatballs back in the

228
00:07:41,856 --> 00:07:43,293
gravy, cover the pan,

229
00:07:43,293 --> 00:07:45,757
and let them simmer gently for about

230
00:07:45,757 --> 00:07:48,563
ten minutes, until they're cooked all the

231
00:07:48,563 --> 00:07:49,385
way through.

232
00:07:49,565 --> 00:07:52,035
Spoon the gravy over them now and

233
00:07:52,035 --> 00:07:52,409
then.

234
00:07:52,589 --> 00:07:55,209
Taste the gravy and add salt and

235
00:07:55,209 --> 00:07:55,782
pepper.

236
00:07:55,962 --> 00:07:57,548
It should be smooth,

237
00:07:57,548 --> 00:07:59,372
creamy and light brown,

238
00:07:59,372 --> 00:08:02,069
the color of coffee with plenty of

239
00:08:02,069 --> 00:08:03,021
cream in it.

240
00:08:03,370 --> 00:08:05,929
So far, bread soaked in milk,

241
00:08:05,929 --> 00:08:08,312
grated onion, a gentle mix,

242
00:08:08,312 --> 00:08:10,165
small even meatballs,

243
00:08:10,165 --> 00:08:11,841
browned in batches,

244
00:08:11,841 --> 00:08:13,518
and a toasty gravy.

245
00:08:13,698 --> 00:08:15,300
And now Mrs.

246
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:17,802
Lindqvist's last secret,

247
00:08:17,802 --> 00:08:19,834
from the icebox door.

248
00:08:20,014 --> 00:08:21,794
Right before serving,

249
00:08:21,794 --> 00:08:25,101
stir a big spoonful of lingonberry jam,

250
00:08:25,101 --> 00:08:26,882
or red currant jelly,

251
00:08:26,882 --> 00:08:28,493
or cranberry sauce,

252
00:08:28,493 --> 00:08:30,358
into the gravy itself.

253
00:08:30,538 --> 00:08:32,593
Just one tablespoon.

254
00:08:32,773 --> 00:08:34,786
It doesn't make it sweet,

255
00:08:34,786 --> 00:08:35,269
honey.

256
00:08:35,449 --> 00:08:37,554
It makes it taste finished,

257
00:08:37,554 --> 00:08:38,723
round and rich.

258
00:08:39,073 --> 00:08:41,966
And that's why she served the jam

259
00:08:41,966 --> 00:08:43,018
on the side,

260
00:08:43,018 --> 00:08:43,369
too.

261
00:08:43,549 --> 00:08:46,533
Sweet and tart with salty and creamy.

262
00:08:46,713 --> 00:08:49,474
You can find lingonberry jam at most

263
00:08:49,474 --> 00:08:51,239
big grocery stores now,

264
00:08:51,239 --> 00:08:54,230
or at that Swedish furniture store with

265
00:08:54,230 --> 00:08:55,304
the cafeteria.

266
00:08:55,484 --> 00:08:58,556
But plain cranberry sauce from the can

267
00:08:58,556 --> 00:08:59,850
works just fine.

268
00:09:00,030 --> 00:09:03,861
I use whatever's left over from Thanksgiving.

269
00:09:04,041 --> 00:09:07,262
My husband finally admitted she hadn't lost

270
00:09:07,262 --> 00:09:08,685
her mind after all.

271
00:09:09,034 --> 00:09:11,250
Serve them over a big pile of

272
00:09:11,250 --> 00:09:14,305
mashed potatoes or buttered egg noodles,

273
00:09:14,305 --> 00:09:15,909
with plenty of gravy,

274
00:09:15,909 --> 00:09:18,277
a spoon of berries on the side,

275
00:09:18,277 --> 00:09:21,027
and a little chopped parsley or dill

276
00:09:21,027 --> 00:09:21,562
on top.

277
00:09:21,742 --> 00:09:23,088
And Mrs.

278
00:09:23,268 --> 00:09:27,480
Lindqvist always served quick pickled cucumbers on

279
00:09:27,480 --> 00:09:30,260
the side, sliced thin in vinegar,

280
00:09:30,260 --> 00:09:31,523
sugar and dill.

281
00:09:31,703 --> 00:09:34,420
They're cool and crisp next to the

282
00:09:34,420 --> 00:09:35,778
warm, rich gravy.

283
00:09:36,128 --> 00:09:37,442
And for a party,

284
00:09:37,442 --> 00:09:40,889
honey, do it the nineteen sixty-seven way.

285
00:09:41,069 --> 00:09:42,921
Make them a little smaller,

286
00:09:42,921 --> 00:09:45,047
keep them warm in a slow cooker

287
00:09:45,047 --> 00:09:45,939
in the gravy,

288
00:09:45,939 --> 00:09:48,134
and put a cup of toothpicks next

289
00:09:48,134 --> 00:09:48,545
to it.

290
00:09:48,725 --> 00:09:50,182
And to freeze them,

291
00:09:50,182 --> 00:09:52,711
cook the meatballs and the gravy,

292
00:09:52,711 --> 00:09:55,623
cool them, and freeze them together in

293
00:09:55,623 --> 00:09:57,770
containers for three months.

294
00:09:57,950 --> 00:10:00,648
Thaw them overnight and warm them gently

295
00:10:00,648 --> 00:10:01,525
on the stove.

296
00:10:01,875 --> 00:10:03,303
So one more time.

297
00:10:03,483 --> 00:10:05,295
Soak white bread in milk.

298
00:10:05,475 --> 00:10:06,670
Grate the onion.

299
00:10:06,850 --> 00:10:08,289
Beef and pork,

300
00:10:08,289 --> 00:10:10,345
nutmeg and allspice.

301
00:10:10,525 --> 00:10:11,584
Mix it gently,

302
00:10:11,584 --> 00:10:13,625
roll them like a baby bird.

303
00:10:13,805 --> 00:10:15,546
Brown them in batches.

304
00:10:15,726 --> 00:10:17,608
Cook the flour golden,

305
00:10:17,608 --> 00:10:20,173
and whisk the broth in slowly.

306
00:10:20,353 --> 00:10:22,757
Cream, and a spoon of jam in

307
00:10:22,757 --> 00:10:23,615
the gravy.

308
00:10:23,795 --> 00:10:25,177
That's Mrs.

309
00:10:25,357 --> 00:10:28,059
Lindqvist's Swedish meatballs,

310
00:10:28,059 --> 00:10:30,941
soft as a pillow and never hard.

311
00:10:31,291 --> 00:10:33,242
Tell me in the comments,

312
00:10:33,242 --> 00:10:34,136
sweetheart.

313
00:10:34,316 --> 00:10:36,256
Jam with meatballs,

314
00:10:36,256 --> 00:10:37,276
yes or no?

315
00:10:37,456 --> 00:10:39,798
I know some of you think we're

316
00:10:39,798 --> 00:10:40,266
crazy.

317
00:10:40,446 --> 00:10:43,684
The whole playlist of Grandma's recipes is

318
00:10:43,684 --> 00:10:45,766
right there on your screen,

319
00:10:45,766 --> 00:10:47,925
and I'll see you in the next

320
00:10:47,925 --> 00:10:48,387
video.

321
00:10:48,567 --> 00:10:50,286
Good night, honey.
